{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Hey, arm out please, I'll grab a blood pressure before Dr. Shah steps in.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): My sister got that arm implant last spring and she will not stop texting me about it. Anyway.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (NURSE): One eighteen over seventy four. Pulse seventy two.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm Dr. Shah. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Birth control.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'm her mom. I drove her so she wouldn't bail.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): What have you used before?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Pill.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): The name, if you've got it?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Yaz.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Five-ish months, then she quit.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): What made you stop?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Headaches.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Still getting them?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any flashing lights or blind spots with them?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Bad enough she missed a whole shift. They quit when the pills quit.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): So headaches on Yaz, bad enough to miss work, gone after you stopped, no flashing lights.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Err, thinking out loud, could've been the estrogen, could've been tension, could've been not enough water. I am not calling it migraine and I won't lock a diagnosis today.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): My working thought is the combined pill set them off. The estrogen can irritate the blood vessels in the head, and that's what kicks the headache off. It does not mean anything in there is damaged.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two cigarettes on weekends if she's out. Drives me nuts.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): List your medicines, what each one is for, and how you take it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Lisinipril ten milligrams mornings for the pressure. Iron once a day for the anemia. Only the ashwaganda powder in the morning.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Back to you. Lisinopril ten milligrams every morning for the pressure, iron once a day for anemia, ashwaganda powder each morning. Anything else?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The iron is sixty five milligrams. She forgets that part.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to drugs or anything else?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Chest pain? Trouble breathing?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): Periods heavy or painful?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Other systems, real quick. Stomach, bladder, mood. Anything off?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (NURSE): Popping in. Chart gets that one eighteen over seventy four. My little boy has his shots down the hall, so I'm ducking out.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (DOCTOR): Pressure today is comfortable. You smoke sometimes, and the combined pill lined up with the headaches, so no estrogen from me. I am not saying every hormone is off the table.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Implant?",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (DOCTOR): That's one option. Nexplanon sits in the arm and releases progestin for about three years. There's also a progestin-only pill every day, or an IUD. I won't pick for you today.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I had an IUD and it was awful. That's me, not her.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (DOCTOR): Here's the implant leaflet to take home. Come back in two weeks and we'll decide. Nothing gets placed today.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): If the headaches come back before then, call us. Otherwise I'll see you in two weeks.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay."
 ],
